# Written by Claude on 20-Oct-26. Expected exit status of return_256.c (see tests/run_e2e.sh).
# 256 doesn't fit in the 8-bit exit status: the parent sees only the low 8 bits (POSIX, wait), so 256 mod 256 = 0.
# The compiler still returns the whole int; the truncation happens outside the program.
0
